"asr": "A satellite photo showed what looked like Amelia Earhart's plane, sitting in a Pacific lagoon. It was first spotted in 2020 on the remote atoll of Nikuma Ro -Rho. Then it turned up in aerial photos from 1938, barely a year after she vanished. In October, 2026, a 17 -person team sailed five days to find out. They surveyed the lagoon with a drone, sonar and a magnetometer that detects steel. On October 19th, they announced the answer. It was not her plane. It was a clump of fallen trees. Most of it had already washed away. Only one Y -shaped piece was left. And the metal shine, a hardened crust of coral sand. They did pull a 30 -inch steel tube from the lagoon, but nobody has tied it to her Elektra. 89 years on. No confirmed wreckage. So where did Amelia Earhart go?"
